    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nWelcome to Kilmore, 14 Willow Grove, a substantial 4 bedroom semi-detached home idylically nestled between Cabinteely, Cornelscourt and Foxrock Villages. Set in a quiet and mature cul-de-sac, No. 14 offers both spacious and well-appointed accommodation 120sq.m (1,294sq.ft) that would be ideally suited to those in search of their first home, and those with a growing family looking to trade up alike.\n\nBuilt circa 1982, this fine property offers many notable features, such as off-street parking for several cars and side access to the West-facing rear garden. The incredibly popular Cabinteely Park, spanning 45 hectares and full of beautifully mature trees and trails, is less than a kilometre from your doorstep.\n\nInternal living accommodation comprises a porch leading through to an entrance hallway with a large front reception/living room to the left, a door to the rear bringing you through to a fantastic dining room, flooded with natural light from its French doors onto rear garden. A spacious kitchen/breakfast room runs parallel to the living room and completes what is a sizeable and well laid out ground floor offering.\n\nOn the first floor there are four generously appointed bedrooms, the main bedroom of which features a rear aspect, wall-to-wall fitted wardrobes and a private en-suite. A family bathroom concludes the floor.\n\nOutside, the front garden offers off-street parking for several cars and a side access leading through to sunny Westerly rear garden, walled and with a mix of patio space and lawn. A block built shed unit houses the oil burner and provides ample outdoor storage space. There is also a well maintained green space for residents to enjoy.\n\nKilmore, 14 Willow Grove boasts a highly desirable cul-de-sac setting, nestled just moments away from Dunnes Stores at Cornelscourt and being within walking distance to the excellent Cabinteely Park, local shops and sporting facilities including Leopardstown Golf Club, Carrickmines Lawn Tennis CLub and Westwood Leopardstown to name but a few. The N11, QBC, M50 and Luas are all close by meaning access to any part of Dublin or indeed further afield is with ease. There are two National schools within walking distance and there are many other renowned schools close by coupled with ease of access to some of South Dublin's highly regarded secondary schools.\n\nOverall, 14 Willow Grove presents a fantastic opportunity for a growing family and viewing is highly advised."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nTiled porch stepped to front door, carpet, window to side entrance, doors to living room and kitchen\n\nLiving Room - \nCarpet, gas fireplace, door to dining room, radiators\n\nDining Room - \nCarpet, breakfast hatch, French doors to garden, door to kitchen, understairs storage, radiator\n\nKitchen - \nTiled, ample counter space and fitted cabinets, door leading to garden, induction hob, stainless steel sink, tiled splashback, radiator\n\nBedroom 1 - \nRear aspect, carpet, fitted wardrobes, en-suite, radiator\n\nBedroom 2 - \nFront aspect, carpet, fitted wardrobes\n\nBedroom 3 - \nFront aspect, carpet, fitted wardrobes\n\nBedroom 4 - \nRear aspect, carpet, radiator\n\nBathroom - \nTiled floor and walls, bath, wc, whb, fitted mirror, window, radiator\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Impressive four bed semi-detached property with side entrance in a prime Dublin 18 location</li><li></li><li>Approx. 120sq.m</li><li></li><li>Sunny West-facing rear garden</li><li></li><li>Mature cul-de-sac setting</li><li></li><li>Short stroll to St Brigids Boys and Girls National Schools</li><li></li><li>Oil fired central heating</li><li></li><li>Close to an abundance of nearby amenities including Dunnes Stores Cornelscourt</ul>"
      },
